# Seconds each test file takes, read by tests/run.sh to start the costliest files first when it runs more than one at a time (GSG_TEST_JOBS > 1),
# and checked by tests/project/test_cost_list.sh (every test file has a line, no line names a missing file). Printing order is not affected.
# Format, one file per line: base name without .sh, Windows seconds, Linux seconds. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# Windows = the seconds a file ran on Windows CI, beside the other files of the run, from the `TIME    <name> <seconds>s` lines tests/run.sh prints in the windows-suite log;
# given for the files over about 100 seconds there and the Windows-only files; - = under that or not measured.
# Linux = the per-file seconds measured on Linux, used on macOS too and as the tie-break on Windows. A file not listed starts first; a malformed line counts as not listed.
# To update a value, read the TIME line of a CI log or time `tests/run.sh FILE`; to add a file, add a line with its measured seconds.
